================================================================================
SCOPE OF THIS LICENCE
================================================================================

The MIT licence above covers the original work in this repository only. Four
categories of material distributed with, referenced by, or produced from this
repository are NOT licensed by the paragraphs above. Nothing here purports to
grant rights in material the authors do not own.

1. THIRD-PARTY SOURCE CODE
   Substantial parts of the training core are derived from third-party projects
   and remain under their own licences, which are compatible with but distinct
   from the grant above:

     - HTS-AT (MIT, Copyright (c) 2022 Knut(Ke) Chen)
     - Microsoft Swin-Transformer (MIT, Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation)
     - PyTorch Image Models / timm (Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2019
       Ross Wightman) - primitives are vendored into
       src/mirasol/models/layers.py and have been modified
     - PANNs / audioset_tagging_cnn (MIT, Copyright (c) Qiuqiang Kong)

   The original copyright headers are preserved verbatim in every derived file.
   Full licence texts, the file-by-file inventory and the Apache-2.0 change
   statement are in THIRD_PARTY.md. Removing those headers - for example by a
   PII or docstring cleanup pass - would breach the licences.

2. THE CirCor DigiScope DATASET
   The CirCor DigiScope Phonocardiogram Dataset is licensed by its authors
   under the Open Data Commons Attribution License v1.0 (ODC-By 1.0) and is
   distributed by PhysioNet. It is NOT redistributed in this repository: no
   CirCor audio file and no CirCor metadata file is committed here. Users must
   obtain it from https://physionet.org/content/circor-heart-sound/ under its
   own terms and must satisfy its attribution requirement independently. See
   data/README.md and docs/data.md.

3. DERIVED DATA COMMITTED IN THIS REPOSITORY (ODC-By 1.0, NOT MIT)
   Two directories contain data derived from CirCor DigiScope and are therefore
   Derivative Databases under ODC-By 1.0 rather than MIT-licensed software:

     results/predictions/   out-of-fold model outputs; each row carries a
                            CirCor recording filename (patient identifier and
                            auscultation location) and the murmur target
                            derived from CirCor's Murmur column
     data/splits/           the patient-to-fold assignment, keyed by CirCor
                            patient identifier

   Anyone redistributing those two directories, or a database derived from
   them, must comply with ODC-By 1.0 and must carry the CirCor attribution
   given in THIRD_PARTY.md section 6. The identifiers involved are already
   public in the CirCor distribution; nothing non-public is added here. Both
   directories carry their own README.md restating this.

4. PRE-TRAINED WEIGHTS OBTAINED FROM UPSTREAM
   The released models were fine-tuned from ImageNet-pretrained backbones whose
   weights are third-party artefacts under their own terms, and the exported
   ONNX graphs are derivative works of those weights:

     - FastViT: every released FastViT graph derives from
       fastvit_t8.apple_in1k. The original implementation and weights are
       Copyright (C) 2023 Apple Inc., All Rights Reserved, released under
       Apple's own licence at https://github.com/apple/ml-fastvit - which is
       NOT the MIT licence. An unqualified MIT claim over those graphs would
       purport to relicense Apple's weights; this licence makes no such claim.
     - TinyViT (tiny_vit_5m_224), MobileNetV3-Small
       (mobilenetv3_small_100.lamb_in1k) and ResNet-18 (resnet18.a1_in1k)
       derive from timm weights (Apache License 2.0).
     - EfficientNet-B0 derives from torchvision
       EfficientNet_B0_Weights.IMAGENET1K_V1 (BSD-3-Clause).
     - HTS-AT is trained from scratch here (no pretrained checkpoint is
       loaded), but the architecture is the MIT-licensed HTS-AT of section 1.

   THIRD_PARTY.md section 5 records Apple's copyright, disclaimer and
   no-endorsement terms in full.

